## 🔥 Use Case: Detect Pods Handling Unusual Load (Too High or Too Low)

---

### ✅ Option 1: **API Request Load Imbalance**

#### 🔍 Metric:

```prometheus
rate(http_requests_total{
  cluster_name="azure-eastus-st-085-np-aks-001",
  namespace="storefront-storefront-ut",
  pod=~"storefront-api-ut-.*"
}[5m])
```

---

#### 🚨 ALERT #1: POD Getting **Too Much Load** (Hot Pod)

```prometheus
(
  rate(http_requests_total{cluster_name="azure-eastus-st-085-np-aks-001", namespace="storefront-storefront-ut", pod=~"storefront-api-ut-.*"}[5m])
)
>
(
  avg by(namespace) (
    rate(http_requests_total{cluster_name="azure-eastus-st-085-np-aks-001", namespace="storefront-storefront-ut", pod=~"storefront-api-ut-.*"}[5m])
  )
) * 2
```

> 📌 This triggers if **any pod gets more than 2× the average traffic**

---

#### 🚨 ALERT #2: POD Getting **Too Little Load** (Stale Pod)

```prometheus
(
  rate(http_requests_total{cluster_name="azure-eastus-st-085-np-aks-001", namespace="storefront-storefront-ut", pod=~"storefront-api-ut-.*"}[5m])
)
<
(
  avg by(namespace) (
    rate(http_requests_total{cluster_name="azure-eastus-st-085-np-aks-001", namespace="storefront-storefront-ut", pod=~"storefront-api-ut-.*"}[5m])
  )
) * 0.5
```

> 📌 Triggers if a pod is handling less than 50% of the average traffic — useful to catch idle or broken pods.

